{"seq":2,"at":"2026-10-20","kind":"edited","target":{"type":"article","id":"a0354"},"reason":"Rewritten by the merge to take in the printed cards' questions.","by":"merge everyday/holidays","ref":"quiz-archive/runs/tp-ingest/decisions/everyday__holidays.json","changes":[{"field":"bodyEn","diff":[["-","On"],["+","The"],["=",1],["-","12"],["+","largest"],["=",1],["+","folk festival in the world began as a royal wedding party. What Munich celebrated in "],["=",4],["+","was the wedding of "],["=",6],["+","and Princess Therese: on 12 October Ludwig "],["=",22],["-","Saxe-Hildburghausen"],["+","Saxe-Hildburghausen."],["=",1],["-","in Munich. "],["=",62],["+","That race is regarded as the forerunner of the festival. "],["=",112],["-","made"],["+","kept"],["=",3],["+","festival growing.\n\nThe idea travelled with Bavaria's emigrants. Blumenau, a town in southern Brazil founded by German settlers in 1850, held its own "],["=",2],["+","for "],["=",2],["-","largest"],["+","first"],["=",1],["-","folk"],["+","time"],["=",1],["+","in 1984 to raise money for rebuilding after the floods of the Itajaí-Açu river. With more than 600,000 visitors a year it has become the second-largest popular "],["=",4],["+","Brazil, surpassed only by "],["=",2],["-","world."],["+","Carnival in Rio de Janeiro."],["=",577],["-","wedding"],["+","wedding,"],["=",1],["+","celebrated with a horse race "],["=",4],["+","Oktoberfest (Blumenau) | 1984 | Brazil | Flood relief |\n| "],["=",181]]},{"field":"bodyDe","diff":[["-","Am"],["+","Das"],["=",1],["-","12."],["+","größte"],["=",1],["+","Volksfest der Welt begann als königliche Hochzeitsfeier. Was München im "],["=",4],["-","heiratete"],["+","feierte,"],["=",1],["+","war die Hochzeit von "],["=",4],["+","und Prinzessin Therese: Am 12. Oktober heiratete Ludwig "],["=",14],["-","in München "],["=",68],["+","Dieses Rennen gilt als Vorläufer des Festes. "],["=",106],["-","haben"],["+","ließen"],["=",3],["-","Oktoberfest"],["+","Fest"],["=",1],["+","immer weiter wachsen.\n\nDie Idee wanderte mit Bayerns Auswanderern. Blumenau, eine 1850 von deutschen Siedlern gegründete Stadt im Süden Brasiliens, feierte 1984 erstmals ein eigenes Oktoberfest, um Geld für den Wiederaufbau nach den Überschwemmungen des Flusses Itajaí-Açu zu sammeln. Mit über 600.000 Besuchern im Jahr ist es "],["=",2],["-","größten"],["+","zweitgrößten"],["=",3],["-","der"],["+","Brasiliens"],["=",1],["-","Welt"],["+","geworden,"],["=",1],["-","gemacht."],["+","übertroffen nur vom Karneval in Rio de Janeiro."],["=",551],["-","Hochzeit"],["+","Hochzeit,"],["=",1],["+","gefeiert mit einem Pferderennen "],["=",4],["+","Oktoberfest (Blumenau) | 1984 | Brasilien | Hilfe nach der Flut |\n| "],["=",165]]}]},
